# Crockpot API — /shopping-list
#
# GET /shopping-list — CROC-021. Behind full AuthMiddleware, same shape
# as /menu. Never writes: a user with no shopping_lists row yet gets 200
# + empty items, no row created. The list itself is a side effect of the
# three /menu/entries write endpoints (CROC-019) — there is no separate
# "regenerate" endpoint to call here, POST/PATCH/DELETE on /menu/entries
# below do that automatically, in the same transaction as the menu write.
#
# POST/PATCH/DELETE /shopping-list/items and DELETE /shopping-list —
# CROC-022 (manual items, obtain-toggle, quantity edit, clear list).
#
# This file creates its own throwaway items + two throwaway recipes
# (both using itemId, no unit — "2 eggs"-style) with the ADMIN account,
# so the shopping list actually has something to aggregate. Run
# top-to-bottom: by the end, both recipes are off the menu again and
# the list is back to empty before Cleanup deletes the fixtures.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Login (ADMIN account)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Fixtures — two items, two throwaway recipes using the first
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Real item category to hang the throwaway items off.
# @name itemCategory
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/item-categories

###

@itemCategoryId = {{itemCategory.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Real seeded recipe category.
# @name recipeCategories
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories

###

@recipeCategoryId = {{recipeCategories.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Throwaway item — no unit involved, keeps this file independent of
### seeded unit ids/order (unit-merging itself is covered by
### internal/repository/shopping_list_test.go's TestRegenerate_* suite).
# @name item
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list-item",
  "categoryId": "{{itemCategoryId}}"
}

###

@itemId = {{item.response.body.id}}

### A second throwaway item, never referenced by any recipe — used below
### for the CROC-022 manual-add walkthrough, kept separate from itemId so
### a GET response never has to disambiguate two same-named rows.
# @name manualItem
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list-manual-item",
  "categoryId": "{{itemCategoryId}}"
}

###

@manualItemId = {{manualItem.response.body.id}}

### recipeA — serves 4, needs 2x the item.
# @name recipeA
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list Recipe A",
  "timeInMinutes": 30,
  "serves": 4,
  "instructions": ["Cook it"],
  "categoryIds": ["{{recipeCategoryId}}"],
  "ingredients": [{ "itemId": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": 2 }]
}

###

@recipeAId = {{recipeA.response.body.id}}

### recipeB — serves 4, needs 3x the same item. Combining with recipeA's
### need for the same item into one summed row is the point of this fixture.
# @name recipeB
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list Recipe B",
  "timeInMinutes": 30,
  "serves": 4,
  "instructions": ["Cook it too"],
  "categoryIds": ["{{recipeCategoryId}}"],
  "ingredients": [{ "itemId": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": 3 }]
}

###

@recipeBId = {{recipeB.response.body.id}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /shopping-list — before anything's added
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — empty items. No error even if this account has never had a
### shopping list, and no row is created by this GET.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Add recipeA to the menu — shopping list regenerates automatically
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — add recipeA at serves 4 (its own serves — scale 1). Lazily
### creates both the menu row and the shopping list row.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{recipeAId}}",
  "serves": 4
}

###

### ✅ 200 — one item, quantity 2 (recipeA's need, no scaling at serves 4/4).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Add recipeB to the menu — combines into the same row
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — add recipeB at serves 4 too.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{recipeBId}}",
  "serves": 4
}

###

### ✅ 200 — still one item (same item, no unit — same combine key),
### quantity now 5 (recipeA's 2 + recipeB's 3). Exactly one row on the
### list at this point, so $[0] below is unambiguous.
# @name listAfterCombine
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

@generatedRowId = {{listAfterCombine.response.body.items[0].id}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  PATCH /shopping-list/items/:id — obtain-toggle (CROC-022)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — tick the combined row obtained.
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items/{{generatedRowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "obtained": true
}

###

### ✅ 200 — obtained is true, quantity unchanged at 5.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Bump recipeA's serves — obtained survives, quantity updates
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — double recipeA's serves to 8 (scale becomes 8/4 = 2).
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serves": 8
}

###

### ✅ 200 — quantity is now 7 (recipeA's 2×2=4 + recipeB's 3), and
### obtained is still true — the earlier PATCH must have survived this
### regenerate, not been reset to false.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Remove recipeA from the menu — item shrinks, doesn't disappear
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — remove recipeA.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — quantity back down to 3 (recipeB's need alone) — same row,
### same id, still obtained true (row updated in place, not
### deleted-and-reinserted).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Remove recipeB too — item disappears entirely
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — remove recipeB. No recipe on the menu needs the item anymore.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — back to empty items.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /shopping-list/items — manual add, and merging (CROC-022)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — add 2 of manualItemId. Not tied to any recipe, so nothing
### to scale/combine yet.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{manualItemId}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

###

### ✅ 200 — exactly one row, quantity 2, isManual true, obtained false.
# @name listAfterManualAdd
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

@manualRowId = {{listAfterManualAdd.response.body.items[0].id}}

### ✅ 200 — add 3 more of the same manual item.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{manualItemId}}",
  "quantity": 3
}

###

### ✅ 200 — still exactly one row (same id as manualRowId above), now
### quantity 5 — a repeat manual add merges by summing, not a new row.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 🚫 400 invalid_item — itemId doesn't exist.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "quantity": 1
}

###

### 🚫 400 invalid_quantity — zero is rejected.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{manualItemId}}",
  "quantity": 0
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  PATCH /shopping-list/items/:id — quantity edit on a manual row
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — edit the manual row's quantity directly (no remove/re-add
### needed).
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items/{{manualRowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 9
}

###

### ✅ 200 — quantity is now 9, obtained is still false (untouched).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 🚫 400 invalid_request — neither field present.
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items/{{manualRowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /shopping-list/items/:id — manual row: plain delete
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — remove the manual row outright.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items/{{manualRowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — back to empty.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Manual add never merges with a generated row for the same item
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — put recipeA back on the menu: one generated row for itemId,
### quantity 2.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{recipeAId}}",
  "serves": 4
}

###

### ✅ 200 — exactly one row for itemId at this point (the manual
### duplicate below doesn't exist yet) — capture its id now, while it's
### still unambiguous, rather than after two same-named rows exist.
# @name listRecipeAOnly
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

@generatedItemRowId = {{listRecipeAOnly.response.body.items[0].id}}

### ✅ 200 — manually add itemId too, the exact same item the generated
### row already covers.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{itemId}}",
  "quantity": 1
}

###

### ✅ 200 — two separate rows for itemId now: the generated one
### (quantity 2, id = generatedItemRowId above) and a new manual one
### (quantity 1) — confirm both are present in the response, not
### combined into one.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /shopping-list/items/:id — generated row: sticky dismissal
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — delete the generated row (id captured above, before the
### manual duplicate existed).
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items/{{generatedItemRowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — only the manual row (quantity 1) remains.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — an unrelated menu change (recipeB, a different item) triggers
### a regenerate. itemId's required quantity is still 2, matching the
### dismissal recorded above, so it must NOT reappear.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{recipeBId}}",
  "serves": 4
}

###

### ✅ 200 — still only the manual itemId row (quantity 1) plus recipeB's
### own item — the dismissed generated row for itemId must not be back.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — remove recipeB again, back to just recipeA on the menu.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — bump recipeA's serves to 8: itemId's required quantity
### changes from 2 to 4, which no longer matches the stale dismissal
### (quantity 2) — the item must reappear as a fresh, unobtained row.
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serves": 8
}

###

### ✅ 200 — itemId's generated row is back at quantity 4, obtained
### false, alongside the still-present manual row (quantity 1).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /shopping-list — clear list (no dismissal memory)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — wipe everything in one call.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — empty.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — re-save recipeA at the same serves (8) to trigger another
### regenerate. Unlike the single-item delete above, clear list wrote no
### dismissal, so itemId's generated row must come straight back.
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serves": 8
}

###

### ✅ 200 — itemId's row is back at quantity 4 — clear list has no
### memory, unlike a single-item removal.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Auth
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### 🚫 401 — no token.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list

###

### 🚫 401 — no token, on a write endpoint too.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "{{itemId}}",
  "quantity": 1
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Cleanup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Reset back to empty before deleting the fixtures underneath it.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes/{{recipeBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{manualItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###
